<title>USA: TAL lays off staff, seeks Chapter 11 filing.</title>
<headline>TAL lays off staff, seeks Chapter 11 filing.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>TAL Wireless Networks Inc said it laid off its entire U.S. staff based in Sunnyvale and Alaska last week and it is preparing to file a bankruptcy petition.</p>
<p>Its chief executive, John Vargo, resigned. The directors of Tetherless Access Asia Ltd, an Australian operating subsidiary, have appointed an administrator to manage the affairs of that company.</p>
<p>TAL was not immediately available to provide further details. Its stock was trading around 0.05, down 0.03.</p>
</text>
